Review this Go accessor against its documented promise: callers may freely mutate the returned records and their payloads without changing the cache.

type Record struct { Name string; Payload []byte }
type Cache struct { records []Record }
func (c *Cache) Records() []Record { return slices.Clone(c.records) }

There are no concurrent writes during the call. Show the smallest correction and one regression check. Preserve the distinction between nil and non-nil empty payloads if your solution would otherwise change it.
